<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Andkhud</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1204</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Andkhud was fought in 1204 near Andkhoy in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, where an army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazmshah">Khwarazmshah</a> Muhammad II, reinforced by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qara-khitai">Qara Khitai</a>, crushed the Ghurid sultan Mu'izz al-Din Muhammad, who escaped with difficulty. The defeat ended Ghurid expansion into Khurasan, destroyed their prestige in the west and encouraged revolts in their Indian territories.</p></div>
